  "label": "Emotional Overwhelm as Stereotype",
  "description": "The visual of a person with a distressed expression, covering their face with their hands, is used to imply that white children are overwhelmed by societal pressures or systemic issues. This visual metaphor is not directly visible in the image but is implicitly referenced in the meme's text and intent. The use of this visual to represent a racialized group's emotional state is a form of stereotyping that relies on real-world knowledge about how emotional distress is culturally interpreted and associated with specific groups.",
